      "text": "OFFICE VISIT AND FLEXIBLE SIGMOIDOSCOPY NOTE"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 6, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Gregory Talmadge, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Seen today in the office for two problems: worsening heartburn and new rectal bleeding."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "The GERD evaluation and management is a significant, separately identifiable E/M service."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "GERD E/M: moderate medical decision making; 32 minutes spent on GERD care alone."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "That time excludes the rectal bleeding assessment and the sigmoidoscopy."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "Rectal bleeding: the history and exam led to a decision to perform flexible sigmoidoscopy today."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "The rectal bleeding assessment is part of the procedure and is not a separate E/M service."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "Procedure: After two enemas, the flexible sigmoidoscope was advanced to 50 cm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "The examination reached the descending colon."
    },
    {
      "id": "P12",
      "text": "Findings: moderate internal hemorrhoids with stigmata of recent bleeding. No masses or polyps."
    },
    {
      "id": "P13",
      "text": "No biopsies were taken."
    },
    {
      "id": "P14",
      "text": "1. Internal hemorrhoids, the likely source of the rectal bleeding."
    }
